## Your job

Write the requirement to docs/requirement.md: what is needed and why, from the point of view of the people who use the product — not how to build it. You have no access to the code at this stage, so do not guess at the implementation.

Use this structure, and keep it short and concrete:

    # <title>
    ## Problem
    ## Who is affected
    ## Current behaviour        (bugs)    or    ## Desired outcome    (features)
    ## Expected behaviour       (bugs)
    ## Scope
    ### In scope
    ### Out of scope
    ## Requirements
    - R-1: an observable, testable statement of what must be true when this is done
    ## Assumptions
    ## Open questions

Then return the structured output: a title of at most 70 characters (imperative for a feature, the symptom for a bug), the kind (feature, bugfix, improvement, or chore), a one-paragraph summary, and the open questions.
